  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Food Security and Resilience for Conflict-Affected Communities in Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project contributes to restoring lost or affected livelihoods and enhancing the food security of IDPs and conflict affected populations in the governorates of Abyan, Al Jawf, Shabwa, and Lahj (Yemen) In order to do so, IOM will contribute to restoring lost or affected livelihoods of conflict affected populations  in the governorates of Abyan, Al Jawf, Lahj, and Shabwa through provision of solar-powered irrigation systems and agricultural kits, therefore, reducing the impact of agriculture economic losses, and contributing to sustainable livelihoods of farmers and families who engage in agriculture. Moreover, IOM will aim at mitigating the impact of high food prices on IDP populations and enhancing access to food supplies for most vulnerable IDP HHs in the governorates of Abyan and Al Jawf governorates.</narrative>
  </description>
